# PYTHON → FPGA-SIM → board

User-visible glass (READY, LOAD/RUN, JS/Canvas, errors) lands in order. Skip a
rung and the machine is fake. Status: [docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md](../../docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md).

1. **PYTHON** bytecode VM — behavioural truth. Fast: same **results** as the
   chip (bytes, numbers, errors), not wall-clock. Do not throttle Python to
   one hardware tick. Parity runs the **serialized ProgramImage**, not a
   `Chunk`/AST the hardware never sees, and not dukpy (`no-dukpy-cheat-native-cpu`).
2. **FPGA-SIM** — Verilator of the **same** `rtl/*.sv` as the `.bin`
   (`never-fake-fpga-sim`). **By inspection, legal SRAM first, then glass.**
   Do not leave combo/dual heaps in a “fix.” Do not run Vivado / `make bit`
   (the user does that). Flatten-later already looped three times.
3. **User F9** FPGA-SIM `(RTL)` — visual play is this, not a snippet PASS.
4. **Board** `.bit` / `.bin` — only after F9 approval. Do not flash to debug a
   gap FPGA-SIM has not closed. Do not start Vivado for a feature PYTHON +
   FPGA-SIM cannot type. ASIC later.

**Titles** `INVADERS.HTML` / `PACMAN.HTML` / `DONKEY.HTML` must LOAD + RUN and
**look the same** on PYTHON then FPGA-SIM (full game, full ASET). HTML binds
keys; RTL delivers raw keycodes. `?NH` is never done. No RTL-only console
verbs. Board-only smoke = parity bug. PYTHON-only → fix RTL, do not weaken
PYTHON. Tests = real titles, not random programs. Do not invent LUT counts
([docs/FPGA_FIT.md](../../docs/FPGA_FIT.md)).

**Standalone intent:** HDMI + keyboard + Pmod stick; UART/JTAG are debug.
Tether mirrors glass; when J15 works, play needs **zero** code changes. This
board is Nexys Video T200 — not A7-100T. StarLite later.

**Agents:** do not run Vivado / `make bit` unless the user asked. Inspect both
execs **and** the parent case against `never-fake-fpga-sim` (opcode comb
drives no ports; no combo `arr[i]` in `casestate` / tasks / `fn_entry()`;
no second heap; **no `mem[i] <=` on Port A arrays** — `stack_wr` /
`vobj_alloc_wr` / `varr_len_wr` / `name_hash_wr` / `vvars_wr` /
`json_putc` / `imgd_we`). New glass must wait for `*_rdata`, never peek.
One stack write per clock (`stack_dual_pend` for FOREACH el+idx). Extra
clocks OK. `sim_server_synth` PASS is not a bitstream. Then glass. Do not
redesign the architecture, merge engines, or ship RTL-only glass. Traces:
`use-existing-traces`.
